body:
### What It Is

Callout is a client-side Fabric mod for Minecraft that helps you never miss important chat messages, nickname mentions, or custom keywords while playing or AFK.

It is useful when:

* you are AFK or focused on another window;
* fast-scrolling server chat makes important messages easy to miss;
* you need immediate audio alerts for staff callouts, personal mentions, or specific server events;
* you want to review recent ping history and see what happened in chat before and after the mention.

### What It Adds

Callout extends the standard Minecraft chat with:

* configurable sound alerts for your nickname and custom keywords;
* support for regular expressions for advanced chat matching;
* separate volume and pitch settings for each trigger;
* a dedicated mention history screen with highlighted ping messages;
* saved chat context around every detected mention;
* persistent history that survives world exits and game restarts.

### Features

The mod includes:

* nickname-based mention detection;
* up to 5 additional custom triggers;
* `Text` and `Regex` trigger modes;
* case-sensitive or case-insensitive matching;
* optional alerts for your own chat messages;
* automatic cleanup of service artifacts and third-party chat tags;
* filtering for technical sender prefixes in singleplayer and LAN;
* 5 messages of context before and 5 messages after each ping;
* mouse wheel navigation and pagination in the history screen;
* persistent storage in `config/callout_history.json`;
* Mod Menu integration for easier configuration.

### Controls & Settings

Open mention history:

* `Ctrl + K` — open the ping history and chat context screen.

Available settings:

* `Enabled`: main toggle for the mod;
* `Case Sensitive`: toggles letter case matching;
* `Ping Own`: enables or disables alerts for your own messages;
* `Main Trigger`: nickname or primary word trigger with custom sound, volume, and pitch;
* `Additional Triggers`: up to 5 extra triggers with `Text` or `Regex` matching.

### Installation

Required:

* Fabric Loader `0.19.0+`
* Fabric API

Recommended:

* Mod Menu, for configuration through an in-game GUI

Important:

* this is a purely client-side mod;
* it does not need to be installed on the server;
* mention history is saved automatically in `config/callout_history.json`.
